      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Sure! Example avatar ID is: \n\navtr_5b8ae237-700d-459e-a6af-8c40e56f70b3\n\nEnable combat if it's not enabled already, then simply do right fist over your shoulder to grab the hammer. Doing left fist while over the lower part of the handle is supposed to enable the aim constraint (or maybe it was a LookAt, don't quite remember tbh) and effectively two-hand the weapon.\n\nI'm fairly confident the issue arises because VRCConstraints don't override each other based on activation order (e.g. the aim constraint overrode some of the rotations on the parent constraint because it was activated after the parent constraint).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
