  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "So with some testing, I've figured out that having an Aim Constraint and a Parent Constraint makes the aim constraint just... not work. Two-handed guns, broken. Two handed melee weapons, broken.\n\nThe two constraints are on the same object in the Unity hierarchy. Toggling the Aim Constraint allows an effective two-handed system, or at least it did. It works in live branch but doesn't in the beta. I can confirm the animation to activate the two-handed system is working otherwise, it's just the Aim Constraint fails to enable (or the Parent Constraint completely overrides the Aim Constraint instead of the most recently activated constraint being the dominant one).",
